/*
 * Miltalk CAMERA KIT - Classifier with TFT display + Feedback Learning
 * Board: ESP32-S3 N16R8 CAM (onboard OV5640)
 * Display: ST7735 TFT, mounted PORTRAIT (128 wide x 160 tall)
 *
 * Two tabs: HOME (avatar drifts in a circle + MILTALK), ML (train/test/reset).
 * Switch tabs: hold BTN_A and BTN_B together.
 *
 * NEW - Feedback learning: after a TEST, the kit asks "Was this right?"
 *   BTN_A = YES (approve: reinforce the predicted class)
 *   BTN_B = NO  (correct it: learn as the other class)
 *   TEST or RESET = skip feedback
 *
 * [ADDED] ESP-NOW weight transfer to the TESTER kit:
 *   Hold ALL FOUR buttons (A + B + TEST + RESET) until "SENDING" appears.
 *   Sends sumA/sumB/countA/countB. Any action accidentally triggered by the
 *   first button of the combo is undone before sending.
 *   Classification, camera, UI and single-button behaviour are unchanged.
 *
 * ARDUINO IDE SETTINGS:
 *   Board: ESP32S3 Dev Module | PSRAM: OPI PSRAM | Flash: 16MB
 *   Partition: Huge APP | USB CDC On Boot: Enabled
 *   esp32 board package 3.x
 * LIBRARIES: Adafruit GFX, Adafruit ST7735 and ST7789
 */

